<!-- ===== FAQ ===== -->
<section id="faq" class="faq">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:800px;">
    <div class="section-title reveal">
      <span class="script-accent">You ask — Lalasea answers</span>
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list reveal">
      <details>
        <summary>Where is Lalasea Bistro in Ha Tien?</summary>
        <p>Lalasea Bistro is on National Road 80 (QL80) in To Chau ward, Ha Tien (An Giang province) — right on the seafront, just a few minutes' drive from central Ha Tien. Tap "Directions" on this website to open Google Maps and get directions to the door.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What are the opening hours? Are you open on holidays?</summary>
        <p>We're open every day, including public holidays and Tết (Lunar New Year). Monday to Friday we open from 08:00, Saturday and Sunday a little earlier from 07:00, and we close at 23:00.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is the menu available in English?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Every dish on the Lalasea menu is listed in both Vietnamese and English, with prices. You can browse all {{ menuanh.trang.length }} pages on our <a href="/en/menu/">Menu</a> page before you come.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do I book a table or a party at Lalasea?</summary>
        <p>Fill in the booking form on this page, or call / message us on Zalo at <a href="tel:+84{{ thongtin.dien_thoai_goi | replace('0', '', 1) }}"><strong>{{ thongtin.dien_thoai | sdtQuocTe }}</strong></a>. For weddings, birthdays and company parties there is a separate pre-order Party Menu tailored to your budget — see <a href="/en/events/">Events</a> for details.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I stay overnight at Lalasea? How much is it?</summary>
        <p>Yes! Lalasea has a glamping area with fully air-conditioned, furnished wooden tents inside the restaurant grounds, just a few dozen metres from the sea. Packages start from <strong>490,000 VND per person</strong> (groups of 5–6, weekdays) and include breakfast and a BBQ – hotpot dinner. Check-in from 14:00, check-out before 12:00 the next day. See the <a href="/en/glamping/">Glamping</a> page for details — call ahead to hold a tent, as there are only a few.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How much do dishes cost at Lalasea?</summary>
        <p>Most main dishes are around <strong>100,000 – 300,000 VND</strong>. Large seafood portions and dishes sold at the day's market price cost more, and staff always tell you the price before you order. All 14 menu pages with prices are on the <a href="/en/menu/">Menu</a> page.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>I don't eat seafood — what else is there?</summary>
        <p>Plenty. Besides seafood the menu has spicy pork ribs, diced beef steak (bò lúc lắc), Vietnamese sizzling beef (bò né), Hong Kong-style salt &amp; pepper chicken cartilage, fish sauce-glazed chicken wings, crispy fried frog, hotpot, rice and lots of other dishes to share — so big groups with different tastes can still eat together. See every dish on the <a href="/en/menu/">Menu</a> page.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Are Lalasea Bistro Camping and Lalasea Bistro the same place?</summary>
        <p><strong>Yes, it's one place.</strong> Lalasea Bistro is an <strong>open-air beachfront restaurant</strong> on National Road 80, To Chau ward, Ha Tien — and inside the restaurant grounds there's a <a href="/en/glamping/">glamping area with air-conditioned wooden tents</a>. Because we serve food and also have places to sleep, booking sites often list us as <em>"Lalasea Bistro Camping"</em>, while maps and social media usually just say <em>"Lalasea"</em>. They all mean the same place, with the same phone number, <strong>{{ thongtin.dien_thoai | sdtQuocTe }}</strong>.</p>
        <p>Table bookings, overnight tents and <a href="/en/events/">weddings and events</a> all go through that one number: eat and sleep in the same grounds.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is Lalasea in Kien Giang or An Giang province?</summary>
        <p>We haven't moved — we're still on National Road 80, To Chau ward, Ha Tien. Before July 2025 Ha Tien belonged to Kien Giang province; after the provinces merged, Ha Tien is now part of <strong>An Giang</strong> province. Only the province name changed — Lalasea's location, directions and phone number are the same.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

